The Tabula Muris data (SMART-Seq) is downloaded from:
https://figshare.com/articles/dataset/Single-cell_RNA-seq_data_from_Smart-seq2_sequencing_of_FACS_sorted_cells_v2_/5829687

This data set includes 20 tissues.

The full list of all the tissues are in this file:
Tabula_Muris_SMART-seq_tissue_list.txt


The website stores both count matrices and Seurat object files. However, the Seurat object is built by Seurat version 2.

In this folder, I created Seurat object (version 4) for each tissue and for all the cells.

The Seurat object for all the Tabula Muris cells: 
full_seurat_object.rds

The Seurat Object for each tissue:
[tissue_name]_seurat_object.rds

I built pre-trained model using scPred for each tissue and all the cells.

The pre-trained model for all the cells:
Tabula_muris_all_default_model.rds

The pre-trained model for each tissue:
Tabula_muris_[tissue_name]_default_model.rds

These models use gene symbol as their gene IDs.
